<title>USA: Japan seeks $400 million in Northrop work.</title>
<headline>Japan seeks $400 million in Northrop work.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan has requested upgrade work totaling about $400 million by Northrop Grumman Corp on 13 E-2C &quot;Hawkeye&quot; military radar aircraft, the U.S. Defense Department said Monday.</p>
<p>The Pentagon said the Grumman-built aircraft, previously bought by Japan, needed radar upgrades to maintain the readiness of Tokyo's extended early-warning radar system and continue inter-operability with U.S. and NATO forces.</p>
<p>The prime contractor on the work would be Grumman Aircraft Corp of Bethpage, N.Y., a unit of Northrop Grumman.</p>
<p>The routine proposal is expected to go through without opposition from Congress.</p>
</text>
